WEBVTT

00:02.680 --> 00:04.480
Lene, let's go.

00:04.480 --> 00:07.230
Of course. But Rae is still...

00:08.710 --> 00:11.860
What in the world is that silly maid doing?

00:12.220 --> 00:14.580
Pick up the pace, Rae Taylor!

00:14.930 --> 00:16.040
Right away!

00:16.040 --> 00:20.040
<i>I reincarnated into an otome game world, 
and I'm now known as Rae Taylor.</i>

00:20.760 --> 00:24.870
<i>Showing my love for my fave, the game's 
villainess, has been tough on me...</i>

00:25.390 --> 00:29.540
<i>but I'm enjoying my life 
as a maid in another world!</i>

02:00.010 --> 02:05.020
<b>Episode 3</b>

02:00.010 --> 02:05.020
<b>My Love Is a Series of Ups and Downs</b>

02:06.720 --> 02:07.890
Check.

02:09.900 --> 02:12.270
Commoner... You...

02:12.270 --> 02:13.340
Not bad.

02:13.340 --> 02:15.530
She actually drove Prince Rod into a corner.

02:15.930 --> 02:18.150
Rae, you're...

02:18.930 --> 02:20.530
pretty good.

02:20.530 --> 02:22.100
Oh, not really.

02:22.100 --> 02:23.830
Don't bother acting humble.

02:23.830 --> 02:26.790
No one but Yu has ever given me 
this much trouble before.

02:26.790 --> 02:28.700
Do you resign?

02:28.700 --> 02:31.960
Hey! Don't be so disrespectful 
toward Prince Rod!

02:31.960 --> 02:33.000
Nah.

02:33.540 --> 02:35.980
You're definitely good.

02:37.400 --> 02:38.800
But...

02:39.550 --> 02:41.300
Checkmate.

02:42.570 --> 02:43.800
You win.

02:45.130 --> 02:48.870
You saw that coming and started playing to 
counter it since halfway through, didn't you?

02:48.870 --> 02:51.310
What, you actually noticed?

02:51.310 --> 02:55.190
Still, I never realized you had such skill.

02:55.190 --> 02:59.400
For real. Do commoners play chess, too?

02:59.400 --> 03:02.580
No, this was my first time actually playing.

03:02.580 --> 03:03.400
What?

03:03.400 --> 03:06.410
Excuse me? You were that good 
on your first time playing it?

03:06.410 --> 03:10.870
I knew the rules. We just never 
had a chess set at home.

03:10.870 --> 03:12.420
What does that mean?

03:13.080 --> 03:14.670
<i>I wasn't lying!</i>

03:14.670 --> 03:16.880
<i>In the otome game </i>Revolution<i>,</i>

03:16.880 --> 03:20.390
<i>there's an AI chess game that you 
can play against the characters...</i>

03:20.390 --> 03:22.680
<i>and I played it like crazy!</i>

03:22.680 --> 03:25.620
You're as full of mysteries as ever.

03:25.620 --> 03:28.560
Just like with our exams the other day.

03:29.470 --> 03:32.140
Well, I'll take my leave now, Prince Rod.

03:32.140 --> 03:34.170
Let's be on our way, Miss Claire.

03:34.170 --> 03:35.450
Y-Yes.

03:35.450 --> 03:37.690
Sure. Let's play again sometime.

03:38.180 --> 03:39.940
And next time, no holding back.

03:41.100 --> 03:44.700
<i>Oh... He knows I was going easy on him.</i>

03:45.110 --> 03:49.730
<i>Darn it. I just can't get Prince Rod's 
affection level to come down.</i>

03:49.730 --> 03:50.860
Commoner!

03:57.760 --> 04:00.190
Prince Yu, would you like some tea?

04:00.190 --> 04:03.090
Prince Yu, try some of these new sweets.

04:04.210 --> 04:05.300
Thank you.

04:10.910 --> 04:13.060
I've got you in check this time!

04:13.480 --> 04:16.280
So that's your move, eh? Well, then...

04:17.970 --> 04:19.820
Queen to F4.

04:21.690 --> 04:24.950
That'll turn the whole game 
around for you, Claire.

04:25.330 --> 04:27.630
Thank you, Prince Yu,

04:27.630 --> 04:31.330
but please don't speak to me during a game.

04:31.330 --> 04:34.160
I would have figured that out on my own.

04:34.160 --> 04:35.330
Sorry about that.

04:36.210 --> 04:38.690
It's just that Rae's being so mean to you.

04:38.690 --> 04:39.340
Huh?

04:39.340 --> 04:40.670
<i>Gulp!</i>

04:40.670 --> 04:41.930
You didn't notice?

04:41.930 --> 04:45.590
Rae is deliberately putting you on the 
offensive to get you where she wants you.

04:45.590 --> 04:46.310
Right?

04:46.310 --> 04:49.470
Have you really been using 
such cowardly tricks?!

04:49.470 --> 04:54.950
Well, no matter how many times we play, 
you're always on the attack, so I just...

04:55.980 --> 04:59.360
Easy, now. How about 
a little change of pace?

05:00.070 --> 05:02.020
Let's play some poker.

05:04.260 --> 05:06.910
Dede, you'll be our dealer.

05:06.910 --> 05:08.480
Certainly.

05:08.480 --> 05:10.880
Sorry to make you come here for this, Misha.

05:10.880 --> 05:11.810
It's all right.

05:11.810 --> 05:13.390
That's right, Prince Yu!

05:13.390 --> 05:15.470
We're all busy people, you know!

05:15.470 --> 05:17.650
Rae, don't be rude!

05:17.650 --> 05:19.980
I'm terribly sorry, Prince Yu.

05:19.980 --> 05:21.880
I'll give her a talking-to later.

05:21.880 --> 05:23.540
Oh, I don't mind.

05:23.540 --> 05:27.390
You're welcome to be a little 
more informal with me, too.

05:27.390 --> 05:30.140
We're all equal at the academy.

05:30.890 --> 05:33.880
Miss Claire, what do you think of that?

05:33.880 --> 05:35.800
Prince Yu and Misha, I mean.

05:35.800 --> 05:37.950
You think there might be 
something between them?

05:37.950 --> 05:42.020
Why are all of your ideas so vulgar?!

05:42.020 --> 05:45.530
<i>These two were actually 
good friends as children.</i>

05:42.420 --> 05:43.770
Right?

05:45.530 --> 05:49.530
<i>They were quite close before 
Misha's family fell on hard times,</i>

05:47.650 --> 05:49.530
Oh! Prince Yu!

05:49.530 --> 05:53.650
<i>and Misha still secretly admires him.</i>

05:56.140 --> 05:58.530
You can swap out cards up to two times.

05:58.530 --> 06:02.540
There are no chips. Whoever has
the strongest hand wins.

06:02.970 --> 06:05.800
<i>Hmm... This isn't bad.</i>

06:05.800 --> 06:08.300
<i>Just one away from a straight.</i>

06:08.680 --> 06:10.440
I'll swap one card.

06:10.790 --> 06:12.140
Two for me.

06:12.550 --> 06:16.560
<i>That's Misha for you. 
She's mastered the poker face.</i>

06:16.560 --> 06:18.190
Say, Rae.

06:18.190 --> 06:22.090
Is it true you were holding back 
during your chess game with Rod?

06:22.090 --> 06:23.130
What?

06:23.130 --> 06:26.750
Rae, did you really hold back 
in a game against Prince Rod?

06:26.750 --> 06:29.950
No, no. Prince Rod was 
giving me too much credit.

06:30.950 --> 06:33.340
You're such an interesting girl, Rae.

06:33.340 --> 06:35.540
But don't hold back in this game, okay?

06:39.080 --> 06:42.010
I would like to swap one card.

06:42.010 --> 06:44.290
<i>Miss Claire is so easy to read!</i>

06:44.290 --> 06:47.090
<i>She obviously has a good hand! 
She's so cute!</i>

06:47.760 --> 06:49.380
I'll stick with these cards.

06:50.720 --> 06:53.580
Okay, let's start the second round.

06:53.580 --> 06:54.720
What'll it be, Rae?

06:54.720 --> 06:58.260
<i>Prince Yu didn't swap out a single card.</i>

06:58.260 --> 07:01.480
<i>He must have a pretty good hand.</i>

07:01.480 --> 07:04.360
<i>Which means a straight won't be enough.</i>

07:04.970 --> 07:06.610
I'll swap them all.

07:08.240 --> 07:10.490
<i>I'm really going for broke here,</i>

07:10.490 --> 07:12.110
<i>but I have to win...</i>

07:12.110 --> 07:15.160
<i>and see Miss Claire's frustrated face!</i>

07:16.740 --> 07:18.760
Okay, time to show our hands.

07:18.760 --> 07:19.750
Rae?

07:19.750 --> 07:22.370
All trash cards. For the pigs.

07:22.370 --> 07:24.500
Luck wasn't on your side, huh?

07:24.950 --> 07:25.960
And you, Misha?

07:26.440 --> 07:28.000
Three of a kind.

07:30.090 --> 07:31.210
And you, Claire?

07:31.210 --> 07:34.510
From the look on your face, 
I'd guess you have a pretty good hand.

07:36.380 --> 07:37.990
It's a full house!

07:37.990 --> 07:40.020
<i>And there's that cute smugness!</i>

07:40.020 --> 07:42.790
Okay, and I'm last.

07:42.790 --> 07:44.020
My hand is...

07:44.800 --> 07:46.320
Four of a kind.

07:47.730 --> 07:50.510
Th-That's incredible, Prince Yu.

07:50.510 --> 07:51.670
<i>Huh?</i>

07:51.670 --> 07:56.410
<i>I'm pretty sure I had an ace 
of hearts in my original hand...</i>

07:56.410 --> 07:59.770
<i>I get it. The dealer is Prince Yu's attendant.</i>

07:59.770 --> 08:02.700
<i>Which means this game was rigged.</i>

08:03.540 --> 08:06.040
Rae, it looks like there's 
something you want to say.

08:06.040 --> 08:07.540
No, not particularly.

08:07.540 --> 08:09.480
<i>You sly prince!</i>

08:11.080 --> 08:13.630
I never expected a reaction 
like that out of you.

08:13.630 --> 08:15.680
You really are interesting.

08:16.060 --> 08:19.750
What is this about? 
Did you do something again?

08:19.750 --> 08:21.720
I haven't done a thing.

08:21.720 --> 08:24.400
Anyway, we should get going now.

08:24.400 --> 08:27.570
<i>If this keeps up, Misha's gonna 
end up on the dark side!</i>

08:37.140 --> 08:38.700
<i>That sound...</i>

08:38.700 --> 08:40.600
Miss Claire!

08:40.600 --> 08:42.390
What's all the fuss about?

08:42.390 --> 08:44.100
Come this way for a second!

08:44.100 --> 08:45.710
Huh? Rae?

08:46.060 --> 08:49.290
Wait, commoner! 
Just where are you taking me?

08:49.290 --> 08:50.340
Shh.

08:50.800 --> 08:52.620
There! Look at that!

08:57.280 --> 08:58.650
Prince Thane!

08:58.650 --> 09:01.540
Oh, what a lovely tune!

09:01.540 --> 09:05.100
<i>This is an event of Prince 
Thane's from the game.</i>

09:05.100 --> 09:07.100
<b>It's nothing worth subjecting others to.</b>

09:05.100 --> 09:09.110
<b>Thane</b>

09:05.620 --> 09:09.770
<i>Prince Thane has an exceptional 
talent for playing the harp.</i>

09:07.150 --> 09:09.110
<b>This is merely a pastime.
It has nothing to do with being a good king.</b>

09:09.150 --> 09:11.360
<b>Thane then put down the harp.</b>

09:09.770 --> 09:12.620
<i>The protagonist praises him for it, but...</i>

09:13.060 --> 09:15.240
That's beautiful, Prince Thane!

09:17.470 --> 09:20.120
It truly touched my heart!

09:20.120 --> 09:22.620
What a wonderful harp performance!

09:22.620 --> 09:24.260
Oh, man!

09:24.260 --> 09:27.120
<i>Miss Claire just did exactly the wrong thing!</i>

09:27.120 --> 09:29.080
<b>Thane</b>

09:27.120 --> 09:29.130
<b>You've been listening, haven't you?</b>

09:27.450 --> 09:30.330
<i>The way to raise his affection 
level the most in this event</i>

09:29.170 --> 09:31.130
<b>Oh, no. I was trying to stay out of the way, but Thane noticed me.</b>

09:30.330 --> 09:33.130
<i>is to keep listening until he finishes 
before approaching him!</i>

09:31.130 --> 09:33.130
<b>Thane</b>

09:31.130 --> 09:33.130
<b>Why didn't you say anything?</b>

09:33.130 --> 09:37.120
<i>Talking to him while he's still 
playing has the opposite effect!</i>

09:33.130 --> 09:37.130
<b>Affection Level for Claire</b>

09:38.890 --> 09:41.400
You're stopping already?

09:41.400 --> 09:44.140
It's nothing worth subjecting others to.

09:44.540 --> 09:46.470
This is merely a pastime.

09:46.880 --> 09:49.650
It has nothing to do with being a good king.

09:49.650 --> 09:54.150
Then would you like to play a game 
that will test your suitability to be king?

09:54.150 --> 09:56.650
Wait a minute! What are you...

09:56.650 --> 09:58.160
Rae Taylor.

09:58.750 --> 10:01.860
What is this game that tests 
one's suitability to be king?

10:01.860 --> 10:03.030
Chess?

10:03.030 --> 10:06.290
No, a much more innovative game! 
And that is...

10:06.760 --> 10:08.700
The king game!

10:09.290 --> 10:11.290
The king game?

10:11.690 --> 10:13.700
We all draw lots with numbers on them.

10:13.700 --> 10:15.800
The one who draws the number 1 is the king.

10:16.370 --> 10:18.090
And the king...

10:18.090 --> 10:20.680
Number X and number Y have to do Z.

10:20.680 --> 10:23.310
...gets to give orders to the others!

10:23.620 --> 10:25.470
Go on, draw your lots.

10:27.560 --> 10:31.630
Will this really tell us if someone 
would make a good king?

10:31.630 --> 10:35.230
Yes! Now, here we go! Ready, and...

10:35.230 --> 10:37.140
Who's the king?

10:37.140 --> 10:38.820
Wait! What was that?

10:39.150 --> 10:41.320
It's part of the game.

10:41.320 --> 10:44.950
You have to say it when the results 
of the draw are revealed.

10:45.340 --> 10:46.580
All of us?

10:46.580 --> 10:47.830
Yes, all of us!

10:47.830 --> 10:49.230
No matter what?

10:49.230 --> 10:50.770
No matter what!

10:52.090 --> 10:53.340
I see.

10:53.340 --> 10:55.840
Okay, all together, everyone!

10:56.260 --> 10:58.860
Who's the king?

11:00.030 --> 11:00.840
So it's me?

11:00.840 --> 11:03.790
Yes, you're the king, Prince Thane.

11:03.790 --> 11:04.970
Give your order.

11:06.190 --> 11:08.630
All right, then...

11:08.630 --> 11:10.980
Numbers two and three must hold hands.

11:10.980 --> 11:12.710
I'm number two!

11:12.710 --> 11:15.480
And I'm number three.

11:15.480 --> 11:17.230
Well, then...

11:18.070 --> 11:21.050
D-Don't touch me in such a weird way!

11:21.050 --> 11:24.900
I don't have a choice. 
The king ordered it, after all.

11:24.900 --> 11:27.180
Your hand is so smooth, Miss Claire.

11:27.180 --> 11:29.500
I didn't order you to go <i>that</i> far!

11:29.500 --> 11:32.370
Enough! Next round! We're moving on now!

11:33.010 --> 11:35.380
Who's the king?

11:35.380 --> 11:37.710
I-It's me.

11:37.710 --> 11:39.870
Oh, it's you, Lene?

11:39.870 --> 11:42.880
Hmm, let's see...

11:42.880 --> 11:47.890
Um, okay... Number four must 
pat number three on the head.

11:47.890 --> 11:50.320
Number four... is me.

11:50.320 --> 11:52.940
I-I'm number three...

11:52.940 --> 11:57.430
I don't think one should touch 
a lady's hair without permission.

11:57.430 --> 12:00.780
I-I don't mind at all, Prince Thane.

12:01.460 --> 12:03.610
Then... please excuse me.

12:11.620 --> 12:13.900
Okay, on to the third round!

12:13.900 --> 12:16.130
Who's the king?

12:16.540 --> 12:18.300
Oh! It's me!

12:18.300 --> 12:21.480
Let's see... All right, then...

12:21.480 --> 12:24.300
I just know she's going to 
give some ridiculous order.

12:26.280 --> 12:28.010
<i>One, two, three...</i>

12:28.010 --> 12:30.390
<i>So Lene is number three?</i>

12:30.700 --> 12:34.090
<i>Rae, what are you thinking?</i>

12:34.940 --> 12:36.420
Cheating?

12:36.420 --> 12:39.680
Yeah. When you or I become the king,

12:39.680 --> 12:42.520
we'll communicate our numbers by blinking.

12:42.520 --> 12:45.910
That will tell us Miss Claire's 
and Prince Thane's numbers, too.

12:45.910 --> 12:49.910
And then I can give an order 
that brings them together!

12:49.910 --> 12:53.020
Oh... I suppose so, but...

12:53.910 --> 12:58.110
<i>Doesn't Rae love Miss Claire?</i>

12:58.420 --> 13:00.630
Okay, I've decided!

13:00.630 --> 13:01.870
So...

13:01.870 --> 13:04.170
Numbers two and four must kiss!

13:15.020 --> 13:17.400
Numbers two and four must kiss!

13:19.070 --> 13:22.030
W-Wait, commoner! You know that order is—

13:22.030 --> 13:23.300
What's this?

13:23.300 --> 13:25.940
The king's orders are absolute.

13:25.940 --> 13:28.030
Now, get a move on!

13:30.770 --> 13:31.720
I get it.

13:31.720 --> 13:33.260
Prince Thane?!

13:33.260 --> 13:34.540
Rae Taylor...

13:35.330 --> 13:39.670
This game has nothing to do 
with being a good king, does it?

13:41.310 --> 13:43.340
Were you mocking me?

13:46.810 --> 13:48.550
Well spotted, Prince Thane.

13:48.550 --> 13:49.800
What?

13:50.200 --> 13:54.680
You're right. This game has nothing 
to do with being a good king.

13:55.120 --> 13:57.310
The true objective of this game

13:57.310 --> 14:00.690
was to see whether or not 
you would realize that.

14:01.210 --> 14:03.200
You were testing me?

14:03.200 --> 14:05.510
I do ask your forgiveness for that.

14:05.940 --> 14:09.790
But you refused to comply 
with an unreasonable order

14:09.790 --> 14:12.950
and successfully identified 
my true intentions.

14:12.950 --> 14:16.880
You truly have what it takes to be a king.

14:19.250 --> 14:20.300
I'm leaving.

14:22.790 --> 14:24.090
Prince Thane!

14:25.730 --> 14:28.360
There won't be a second time, Rae Taylor.

14:31.590 --> 14:32.970
Rae...

14:32.970 --> 14:35.010
Was that really true?

14:35.010 --> 14:36.860
Nope, I was lying.

14:36.860 --> 14:39.660
C-Commoner! You...

14:39.660 --> 14:43.800
Miss Claire, how did it feel to have 
Prince Thane pat you on the head?

14:54.950 --> 14:56.490
So, Rae...

14:56.490 --> 14:59.750
Are you what they call "gay"?

15:01.780 --> 15:06.630
Miss Misha, I don't think such topics 
should be discussed so openly...

15:06.630 --> 15:10.380
That's going to make a mess, 
no matter how you approach it...

15:10.710 --> 15:13.430
I don't mind talking about it.

15:13.430 --> 15:14.760
You want to know?

15:14.760 --> 15:17.770
As your best friend, I am curious.

15:17.770 --> 15:20.770
Hmm... Well, I guess...

15:21.350 --> 15:23.520
I probably am, yeah.

15:23.520 --> 15:26.820
I've never been in love with a guy before.

15:29.040 --> 15:31.240
Miss Claire, what's the matter?

15:31.240 --> 15:33.660
I sense that I'm in danger! That's what!

15:34.030 --> 15:38.990
I can see why you wouldn't trust Rae 
based on the things she says and does,

15:39.340 --> 15:42.420
Miss Claire, but to react that way 
just because she's gay

15:42.420 --> 15:45.690
might be said to show a bit 
too much prejudice.

15:45.690 --> 15:46.520
Huh?

15:46.920 --> 15:50.920
For example, you are straight, correct?

15:50.920 --> 15:52.430
Of course I am.

15:52.430 --> 15:55.180
And you love Prince Thane, right?

15:56.930 --> 15:59.280
Rae, don't butt in just to tease her.

15:59.650 --> 16:05.560
Ahem. Miss Claire, how would you feel 
if a man told you, "Don't molest me"?

16:05.560 --> 16:08.910
Wha... I'm not such a lecherous woman!

16:08.910 --> 16:10.070
Of course not.

16:10.070 --> 16:15.070
But what you said to Rae a moment ago 
was the same sort of thing.

16:16.340 --> 16:19.080
Yeah. Misha's right.

16:19.430 --> 16:23.710
No one just lusts after anyone, anytime.

16:24.090 --> 16:28.590
Whether you're gay or straight 
doesn't change that.

16:29.210 --> 16:31.720
Well... That's true...

16:31.720 --> 16:35.380
N-Now, now! Gender doesn't 
matter when it comes to love!

16:35.380 --> 16:39.050
The one you fell in love with just 
happened to be a woman, right?

16:39.050 --> 16:41.180
No, that's not right.

16:41.180 --> 16:43.860
Gender does play a role.

16:43.860 --> 16:46.020
What? It does?

16:46.020 --> 16:47.060
Yeah.

16:47.060 --> 16:52.650
Logically speaking, it might be correct to say 
gender doesn't matter if you love someone,

16:53.050 --> 16:56.910
but at the very least, 
I'm never going to fall for a man.

16:57.330 --> 17:00.080
I guess there are all kinds 
of prejudices out there...

17:00.080 --> 17:03.410
Some people never have a chance 
to learn. They can't help that.

17:03.410 --> 17:07.780
I'm happy just to be able to 
admire Miss Claire every day!

17:07.780 --> 17:11.010
So, Miss Claire, want to 
get lovey-dovey with me?

17:11.010 --> 17:12.620
I do <i>not</i>!

17:12.620 --> 17:16.800
And it's because you're always like this 
that I keep my guard up around you!

17:16.800 --> 17:20.060
I do agree with every part of that.

17:20.060 --> 17:21.960
Aw, why?!

17:22.470 --> 17:26.600
Well, it's not like my feelings 
are ever reciprocated, anyway.

17:26.600 --> 17:27.810
Besides...

17:29.150 --> 17:30.820
What is it, Rae?

17:32.130 --> 17:34.330
Nothing. Never mind.

17:34.330 --> 17:38.570
<i>I'm not the only one who's had 
painful romantic experiences.</i>

17:38.570 --> 17:42.830
Does that mean you've 
given up on Miss Claire?

17:42.830 --> 17:47.700
<i>How am I supposed to feel while 
listening to this conversation?</i>

17:48.050 --> 17:50.590
A-Actually, I thought it was strange, too.

17:51.030 --> 17:55.630
I was sure you were in love with Miss Claire,

17:55.630 --> 17:59.590
but then you cheated in that game 
to bring her and Prince Thane together.

17:59.590 --> 18:03.920
Hey! I think I just heard 
a statement I can't overlook!

18:04.960 --> 18:06.600
I didn't say anything.

18:06.600 --> 18:12.360
Well, yeah... I guess you could say 
I've given up on her, maybe.

18:12.780 --> 18:18.610
But it's more like I never expected her 
to accept my feelings in the first place.

18:18.610 --> 18:23.120
Miss Claire has someone she loves, 
and I want to support her in that.

18:23.510 --> 18:26.990
Besides, I'm happy just being around her.

18:27.370 --> 18:28.990
<i>And above all...</i>

18:29.500 --> 18:34.500
<i>It's not as if getting together 
with Miss Claire is my end goal.</i>

18:35.350 --> 18:37.920
<i>I just want to make her happy.</i>

18:38.510 --> 18:39.580
<i>So...</i>

18:41.470 --> 18:42.510
But still...

18:42.510 --> 18:47.020
If you're asking whether I can 
give up on something I enjoy...

18:48.350 --> 18:50.760
I'm afraid I can't.

18:52.020 --> 18:53.120
Rae...

18:55.920 --> 18:57.530
Just kidding!

18:57.930 --> 19:02.790
So yeah, Miss Claire, just treat me 
the way you always have!

19:02.790 --> 19:04.410
R-Right...

19:04.820 --> 19:08.740
I'm fairly happy with 
our relationship as it is!

19:11.170 --> 19:14.170
Beef bowls! Extra-large servings!

19:14.580 --> 19:16.070
Beef bowls?!

19:16.070 --> 19:19.280
<i>Talking about all those complicated 
subjects made me hungry!</i>

19:19.280 --> 19:21.070
<i>I'm gonna go get a beef bowl!</i>

19:21.070 --> 19:22.440
Oh, for me, too!

19:22.440 --> 19:23.550
I'd like one, too.

19:23.550 --> 19:26.430
Beef bowls acquired!

19:26.430 --> 19:28.700
Didn't you want one, Miss Claire?

19:28.700 --> 19:30.190
No, thank you.

19:31.690 --> 19:34.190
<i>Everything's definitely as it was before.</i>

19:34.710 --> 19:35.600
<i>Yeah...</i>

19:35.940 --> 19:39.690
<i>Just like always, 
it feels just a little bit...</i>

19:40.420 --> 19:41.550
<i>painful.</i>

19:42.200 --> 19:46.860
<i>I've almost never had anyone 
I loved return my feelings.</i>

19:47.200 --> 19:50.430
<i>As long as I don't say anything, 
I can stay close to them,</i>

19:50.430 --> 19:54.710
<i>but the moment I fall in love, 
they're farther away than anyone.</i>

19:57.100 --> 19:59.210
Hey, that commoner...

19:59.210 --> 20:03.720
Yeah, she's the one the rumors say has been 
wooing Miss Claire, even though she's a girl.

20:04.290 --> 20:09.140
<i>Maybe my behavior has been 
encouraging their prejudice.</i>

20:09.720 --> 20:12.410
And I'm sure the princes only like her

20:12.410 --> 20:15.730
because she's so unusual 
that she piques their interest.

20:15.730 --> 20:19.720
Who would ever actually like 
someone as shameful as her?

20:20.190 --> 20:21.350
<i>But...</i>

20:21.760 --> 20:25.740
<i>Making jokes and laughing things off 
is the only way I can get by.</i>

20:32.790 --> 20:35.070
Oh, dear! I'm so sorry!

20:35.070 --> 20:36.580
M-Miss Claire...

20:37.330 --> 20:40.630
I wasn't paying attention, 
and my hand slipped.

20:40.630 --> 20:42.580
You aren't hurt, are you?

20:42.580 --> 20:44.340
Y-You did that on pur—

20:44.340 --> 20:46.820
You aren't, are you?

20:47.260 --> 20:48.350
No...

20:49.840 --> 20:50.750
Commoner!

20:50.750 --> 20:52.100
Y-Yes?

20:52.100 --> 20:54.320
Why are you still dawdling?

20:54.320 --> 20:56.980
If you're finished eating, let's go!

21:01.810 --> 21:04.960
I never thought Miss Claire 
would stand up for Rae.

21:06.490 --> 21:09.220
I wouldn't call that standing up for her.

21:09.220 --> 21:10.120
Huh?

21:10.530 --> 21:12.170
I think Miss Claire couldn't excuse the fact

21:12.170 --> 21:15.570
that she had unintentionally 
done something wrong,

21:15.570 --> 21:18.130
and it left her feeling ill at ease.

21:19.520 --> 21:23.130
And then two girls saying 
mean things just happened by.

21:23.420 --> 21:27.890
What better target for her 
on which to take out her anger, right?

21:28.230 --> 21:30.890
Miss Claire is just a child, really.

21:36.020 --> 21:38.930
This pickled ginger is too sour to eat.

21:38.930 --> 21:42.060
What? But isn't that 
what makes it delicious?

21:42.930 --> 21:44.410
Miss Claire!

21:46.420 --> 21:49.570
What is it? Do you have a problem?

21:49.570 --> 21:53.040
No, it's not that... I just...

21:53.990 --> 21:59.040
You... hate me, don't you?

22:01.500 --> 22:03.550
Of course I do!

22:11.850 --> 22:15.110
But I still love you!

23:46.690 --> 23:49.260
Now to practice my magic for next week!

23:49.260 --> 23:52.770
Oh, so even a dual caster 
needs to prepare, then?

23:52.770 --> 23:55.690
Even with protag specs, 
I still can't spare any effort!

23:55.690 --> 23:58.710
Love, effort, victory! 
So on that note, give me your love!

23:58.710 --> 24:00.530
I don't know what you're talking about!

23:59.500 --> 24:01.000
<b>Episode 4</b>

23:59.500 --> 24:01.000
<b>When Monsters Attack,
Unpreparedness Is the Greatest Enemy</b>
